    "title": "Learn the parts, not the rule",
    "body": "For these verbs there is no rule: the aorist of λέγω is εἶπον, of ἔρχομαι ἦλθον, of ὁράω εἶδον, of φέρω ἤνεγκα. Drill them by principal part until εἶδεν simply reads as 'he saw'. They are the verbs that carry every Gospel story.",
