   "rule": {
    "title": "Root aorists and passive deponents",
    "body": "A few verbs have 'root aorists' with no connecting vowel: ἔγνων (I knew), ἔβην (I went), ἔστην (I stood). Another group takes an aorist passive form with active meaning: ἀπεκρίθη, ἐπορεύθη, ἐφοβήθη, ἐχάρη. Keep drilling until each form triggers its meaning without analysis.",
